import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.DSM5b.PerfComplexDefs
import Submission.Work.DSM5b.H0Defs
import Submission.Work.DSM5b.Basic
import Submission.Work.DSM5b.phiPC_properties
import Submission.Work.DSM5b.rootKillTransport
import Submission.Work.DSM5b.rootKillingFromZeroRoot

/-!
# `Work.DSM5b.orbitKill` — the `φ`-orbit criterion for root killing

Let `R` be perfect of characteristic `p`, `t : ι → R` finite, `T ∈ R`, `t j₀ = T ^ e`, and let
`PCX p t ·`/`PCd p t ·` be the explicit perfected chart Čech complex
(`Submission.Work.DSM5b.PerfComplexDefs.lean`), with the componentwise `p`-th power map `phiPC`
(iterated: `phiPow p t · E`) and its inverse `psiPow p t · E`
(`Submission.Work.DSM5b.rootKillTransport.lean`).

## The criterion

The main point of this file is that **root killing of the perfected complex reduces to a uniform
bound along the single `φ`-orbit of a cycle**:

> if a cycle `z` of `PCX p t (n+1)` satisfies `T ^ N • φ^E (z) ∈ range (PCd p t n)` for one fixed
> `N` and *all* `E`, then `T • z ∈ range (PCd p t n)`.

The proof is the elementary "clear the excess power by taking a root" argument: choose `E` with
`p ^ E ≥ N` and apply `psiPow p t · E` to the relation `T ^ N • φ^E z = d y`.  Since `ψ^E` is
`R`-semilinear (`psiPow_smul`), converts `φ^E z` back to `z` (`psiPow_phiPow`) and commutes with
`PCd` (`psiPow_PCd`), it produces `(T^(1/p^E))^N • z = d (ψ^E y)`; and because
`T = (T^(1/p^E))^(p^E)` with `p^E ≥ N` one may multiply by the complementary power
`(T^(1/p^E))^(p^E - N) ∈ R` to obtain `T • z = d ((T^(1/p^E))^(p^E - N) • ψ^E y)`.

This is *strictly* what the node M5b needs: the DESIGN's "Frobenius upgrade" fails for a *single*
relation `(ϖ k)^m z = d y` (the `ψ`/`φ` moves are information free there), but a uniform bound
along the whole orbit is exactly the extra information that makes the upgrade work.

## Why the orbit bound is the right hypothesis

`Work.DSM5b.orbitUniform` (a separate node) supplies the orbit bound.  Its own proof is
"support + Noetherian": a cycle `z` of `PCX p t ·` has finitely many components, each a finite
polynomial expression in finitely many elements of `R`, so `z` lies in the subcomplex generated by
a *finitely generated* (hence Noetherian) subring `R₀ ⊆ R`; over `R₀` the Noetherian uniform
honest killing (`Work.DSM5b.honestKillCoordNoeth`) gives a *single* exponent `N₀` killing every
cycle of `HCX`, in particular all the honest elements `φ^E z` (`E ≫ 0`); and for the finitely many
remaining `E` the per-cycle honest power killing (`Work.DSM5b.honestPowerKilling`, which is
hypothesis-free) provides the bound.  The natural inequality `killExp w ≤ killExp (φ w)`
(see `killExp_le_killExp_phi` below) fills the gap for small `E`.

Note that the *uniform over `E`* bound is essential: the naive bound obtained by applying `φ^E` to
a level-`0` relation grows like `p^E` and gives nothing.
-/

namespace Work.DSM5b

open Work.DSM5b.Work.DSM5b

universe a

variable (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] {R : Type a} [CommRing R] [CharP R p] [PerfectRing R p]
  {ι : Type a} [Finite ι] [DecidableEq ι] (t : ι → R)

/-- **The `φ`-orbit criterion.**  If a cycle `z` of the explicit perfected chart Čech complex is
`T ^ N`-killed *uniformly along its whole `p`-power orbit* `E ↦ φ^E z` — one exponent `N` for all
`E` — then `T` itself kills `z`. -/
theorem orbitKill_of_uniformOrbit (T : R) (n : ℕ) (z : PCX p t (n + 1))
    (h : ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ E : ℕ, T ^ N • phiPow p t (n + 1) E z ∈ LinearMap.range (PCd p t n)) :
    T • z ∈ LinearMap.range (PCd p t n) := by
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := h
  -- an exponent large enough that the `p ^ E`-th power dominates `N`
  obtain ⟨E, hE⟩ : ∃ E : ℕ, N ≤ p ^ E :=
    ⟨N, le_of_lt (Nat.lt_pow_self (Fact.out : p.Prime).one_lt : N < p ^ N)⟩
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hN E
  -- the root-transported relation
  have key : (((frobeniusEquiv R p).symm)^[E] T) ^ N • z = PCd p t n (psiPow p t n E y) := by
    have h2 := congrArg (psiPow p t (n + 1) E) hy.symm
    rw [psiPow_smul, psiPow_phiPow, psiPow_PCd, iterate_frobSymm_pow] at h2
    exact h2
  refine ⟨(((frobeniusEquiv R p).symm)^[E] T) ^ (p ^ E - N) • psiPow p t n E y, ?_⟩
  rw [map_smul, ← key, ← mul_smul, ← pow_add, Nat.sub_add_cancel hE,
    iterate_frobSymm_pow_eq p T E]

/-- **The `φ`-orbit criterion, unwrapped.**  From a uniform bound along the `φ`-orbit of every
positive-degree cycle of `PCX p t ·` one obtains root killing of `PCX p t ·` at every level `k`. -/
theorem pcxRootKilling_of_orbit (T : R) (j₀ : ι) (e : ℕ) (hj₀ : t j₀ = T ^ e)
    (hOrbit : ∀ (n : ℕ) (z : PCX p t (n + 1)), PCd p t (n + 1) z = 0 →
      ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ E : ℕ, T ^ N • phiPow p t (n + 1) E z ∈ LinearMap.range (PCd p t n)) :
    ∀ (k n : ℕ) (z : PCX p t (n + 1)), PCd p t (n + 1) z = 0 →
      ∃ y : PCX p t n, ((frobeniusEquiv R p).symm^[k] T) • z = PCd p t n y :=
  rootKillingFromZeroRoot p t T j₀ e hj₀ fun n z hz => by
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := orbitKill_of_uniformOrbit p t T n z (hOrbit n z hz)
    exact ⟨y, hy.symm⟩

end Work.DSM5b
